# Browserslist configuration for the frontend build system
# This file instructs build tools (Angular, Autoprefixer, Babel, etc.) which browsers to support.
# Keep the query lines below unchanged to preserve build output and behavior.
#
# Helpful links:
#  - Browserslist query format: https://github.com/browserslist/browserslist#queries
#  - Angular browser support guidance: https://angular.io/guide/browser-support
#
# Environment-specific overrides
#  - You may create environment-specific files (for example: .browserslistrc.dev, .browserslistrc.prod)
#    and load/merge them in your build pipeline if you need different targets per environment.
#
# Security and operational guidance (non-functional comments only):
#  - Do NOT keep insecure "AllowAll" CORS policies in production. Configure CORS on the backend
#    to allow only specific, trusted origins.
#  - Implement authentication (JWT or secure cookie-based sessions) on backend endpoints and
#    apply role-based authorization policies for controller endpoints. Protect authentication
#    cookies with HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite settings and rotate/expire tokens as appropriate.
#  - Store environment-specific sensitive settings (allowed origins, signing keys, secrets) in
#    secure configuration/secrets storage and never check them into source control.
#
# Note: Comments above are guidance only and do not change the behavior of the build.

last 1 Chrome version
last 1 Firefox version
last 2 Edge major versions
last 2 Safari major versions
last 2 iOS major versions
Firefox ESR
not IE 9-10 # Angular support for IE 9-10 has been deprecated and will be removed as of Angular v11. To opt-in, remove the 'not' prefix on this line.
not IE 11 # Angular supports IE 11 only as an opt-in. To opt-in, remove the 'not' prefix on this line.
